		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5001&amp;p=37737#p37737"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>I hope somebody could auditing the source code could find where the issue is and fix it, because is being really annoying, especially with Motorola repeaters that have various TG in different slots.</div></blockquote>Try installing the older betas and find the version where this problem first started to happen</div></blockquote>btw the issues seems that even occurs with the R20240908 stable, so no idea where it could have started, and no idea how much back can I go with the firmware versions because this is with a MD-UV390 Plus.</div></blockquote>Hmmm ok so then perhaps it was whatever I had installed when I got my DM1701, back in april 2024...<br><br>...but I cannot really tell. I've used DMR intensively only since I had my hotspot like 6 months ago. Before, not so much.<br><br>What is clear is that the issue lies in the fact that the DM1701's hardware does not monitor two timeslots, and there is a software solution for that that, given the right conditions, goes awry.<br><br>Which was the stable version back then? did it have the issue? maybe we can start from there<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6012">EA4IAU</a> — Fri Jul 18, 2025 7:19 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
